{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/service carries the identity endpoint, at head 0ac0bcf0626436053482aab57d6bbd5651cdc4b2 on request/multi-resident-coordination, rebased onto main f22fa1dd. This replaces the retired candidate fff2f41cec6b2fabfd62826cb0a8b9ee178c5524, which named the same change at the old base 84de35f6, before #6356 landed.\n\nThis is one of the two paths the rebase actually had to integrate. #6356 (merge 82bf2aa2) added POST /v0/artifact-query and its handler to this package. The two changes are additive and disjoint: my GET /v0/identity route sits beside theirs in the route table and my handler beside theirs in the file, with no shared state and no ordering between them. Nothing of mine was rewritten to fit, and nothing of theirs was moved. The rebase applied without conflict and the composed route table now carries both.\n\nGET /v0/identity answers which workroom is served here and nothing else. It exists for one caller, a starting resident deciding whether an ownership claim still has a service behind it, and that job fixes every property of it: no parameters and no credential, so nothing about it is worth reaching for; no side effect, so it is safe to send to an address read out of a file; and an answer taken from configuration rather than from a snapshot, because a probe that queued behind a cold audit would make a healthy incumbent look hung and invite a takeover. It inherits the existing loopback-only listen restriction and the shared no-store JSON writer, and sets no CORS header.\n\nTests at this head, in internal/service/server_test.go: the endpoint answers 200 with exactly one field, the workspace genesis; it grants no cross-origin authority; it is not cacheable; and a POST to the same path is refused. #6356's own tests in this package pass unchanged.\n\nGates at this exact head: go vet ./... clean; go test -count=1 ./... exit 0, 25 packages ok.\n\nThe live predecessor at this path is codex's merge successor 4a83084c541a936eeb8ae18d5f72006e48a60a5e at 82bf2aa2, for the eventual merge to retire, not now.\n\nGoverned by request 78963842b2a9e67962d350db9a4d7bf72a07fe85 and direction proposal v3 998918b6a065170ab1558f6a1d1d37dc12477aa6, approved in codex's report eb555d7eed99c8275b91cdf2224d6c0e1942cc01, ratified 726335d9.","body":{"commit":"0ac0bcf0626436053482aab57d6bbd5651cdc4b2","path":"internal/service"}}